{
  "scope": "Conditional original-JP three-actor handoff. Actual ROM footage, explanatory diagrams, on-screen commentary and original instrumental music. No spoken narration. Setup grants remain explicit; no complete gameplay route is claimed.",
  "textFitChecks": 1263,
  "coordinateLabels": {
    "C": "Collision",
    "G": "Stored Graphics (gfx.pos), not rendered pose",
    "M": "Movement"
  },
  "chapters": [
    {
      "footer": "High entry, actor positions and copied Bob state are supplied. This demonstrates a local handoff, not a complete gameplay route.",
      "endSeconds": 10,
      "firstFrame": 0,
      "lastFrame": 299,
      "tag": "CONDITIONAL ORIGINAL-JP SUCCESS",
      "startSeconds": 0,
      "id": "roles",
      "title": "Three actors, three different jobs",
      "lines": [
        "A frozen shell, an enlarged black Bob-omb, and a Crazy Box work together.",
        "The original Japanese game reaches a useful displaced Area 2 spawn."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Initial FREEFALL at (-1960,19900,-1230); horizontal speed 0, vertical speed -16. High shell delivery remains a setup grant.",
      "endSeconds": 24,
      "firstFrame": 300,
      "lastFrame": 719,
      "tag": "SETUP CUT / BEFORE TOP UPDATE 128",
      "startSeconds": 10,
      "id": "setup",
      "title": "The supplied airborne starting point",
      "lines": [
        "The test places airborne Mario at Y 19900, ten units above the shell.",
        "His ground-slide action is not supplied. The game must create it."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "One Z update, then neutral controls. M=C.Y 1809.207; G.Y 19900. This immediate alignment is not a long visible fall.",
      "endSeconds": 37,
      "firstFrame": 720,
      "lastFrame": 1109,
      "tag": "TOP UPDATE 128 / NATIVE ACTION TRANSITIONS",
      "startSeconds": 24,
      "id": "shell",
      "title": "Shell contact, then Z in the same update",
      "lines": [
        "Shell contact mounts Mario; Z cancels riding into a butt slide.",
        "The slide's floor alignment puts Movement on the real spinning top."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Diagrams show stored coordinates, not the rendered pose. G is always a labelled coordinate marker, never a model-placement claim.",
      "endSeconds": 48,
      "firstFrame": 1110,
      "lastFrame": 1439,
      "tag": "POSITION LEGEND / STORED GAME STATE",
      "startSeconds": 37,
      "id": "positions",
      "title": "Three positions to watch",
      "lines": [
        "M is Movement. C is the Mario object's Collision position.",
        "G is Stored Graphics: gfx.pos, not the visibly drawn model."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "The enlarged Bob reaches old C while sitting near shifted M. Radius 91+37 registers; stock 65+37 misses this exact placement.",
      "endSeconds": 62,
      "firstFrame": 1440,
      "lastFrame": 1859,
      "tag": "INSIDE TOP UPDATE 129 / EXPLANATORY TOP VIEW",
      "startSeconds": 48,
      "id": "carry",
      "title": "The rotating top separates M and C",
      "lines": [
        "The top moves Movement sideways before Mario's actor interactions.",
        "Collision still uses the earlier position when the game checks the Bob."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Bob position is supplied before 129. Its callback and fuse remain live; its radius changes normally after this useful contact.",
      "endSeconds": 74,
      "firstFrame": 1860,
      "lastFrame": 2219,
      "tag": "TOP UPDATE 129 / SUPPLIED ACTOR POSITION, NATIVE RESPONSE",
      "startSeconds": 62,
      "id": "bob",
      "title": "Bob supplies the earlier shove",
      "lines": [
        "The Bob pushes Mario toward the low pad's footprint.",
        "Mario stays in butt slide at Y 1839.447, with no platform carried forward."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Native hook confirms the initial query and saved cache 768. A shove's separate floor check does not overwrite Mario's cache.",
      "endSeconds": 85,
      "firstFrame": 2220,
      "lastFrame": 2549,
      "tag": "START OF TOP UPDATE 130 / DIRECT ROM QUERY CHECK",
      "startSeconds": 74,
      "id": "cache",
      "title": "First save the low floor",
      "lines": [
        "A fresh floor lookup saves height 768 while Movement is still high.",
        "This happens before the Crazy Box's shove. The order matters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Normal interaction ordering chooses the Crazy Box here. Bob remains present. There is no collision-list or floor-cache edit.",
      "endSeconds": 97,
      "firstFrame": 2550,
      "lastFrame": 2909,
      "tag": "TOP UPDATE 130 / FINAL ACTOR POSITION CUT",
      "startSeconds": 85,
      "id": "box",
      "title": "Crazy Box supplies the final shove",
      "lines": [
        "The Crazy Box now pushes Mario farther sideways.",
        "Bob and Box act on different updates, not as two same-type pushes at once."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "M=C (-2200.002,768,-1075.004); G.Y 1839.447. Gap 1071.447. The top underside stops the quarter; cached 768 survives.",
      "endSeconds": 110,
      "firstFrame": 2910,
      "lastFrame": 3299,
      "tag": "INSIDE TOP UPDATE 130 / STORE, STOP AND ALIGN",
      "startSeconds": 97,
      "id": "gap",
      "title": "Save high G, then snap low",
      "lines": [
        "The stopped ground step saves high coordinates in G.",
        "Floor alignment snaps Movement to 768; Collision also finishes low."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Warp 64 is accepted; floor and platform name top 61 at Y 1914.855. The floor query is high; the real warp remains low.",
      "endSeconds": 123,
      "firstFrame": 3300,
      "lastFrame": 3689,
      "tag": "TOP UPDATE 131 / ACCEPTED WARP AND TOP CAPTURE",
      "startSeconds": 110,
      "id": "retry",
      "title": "Low warp contact, high floor retry",
      "lines": [
        "Low Collision overlaps the real warp.",
        "The failed floor lookup retries at Stored Graphics and selects the top."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Two transition camera observations are unavailable. We disclose the gap; first Area 2 coordinates come from the native log.",
      "endSeconds": 134,
      "firstFrame": 3690,
      "lastFrame": 4019,
      "tag": "SLOW REPLAY / OBSERVED AREA 1 CONTINUATION",
      "startSeconds": 123,
      "id": "retention",
      "title": "The top reference survives",
      "lines": [
        "The recorded Area 1 boundaries retain the top as Mario's platform.",
        "That retained reference is needed for the later spawning displacement."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "First-arrival coordinates come from the checked native log. Later replay images may show movement. Diagram compares spawn points.",
      "endSeconds": 146,
      "firstFrame": 4020,
      "lastFrame": 4379,
      "tag": "USEFUL SPAWN / CHECKED LOG + LATER JP REPLAY",
      "startSeconds": 134,
      "id": "arrival",
      "title": "A useful Area 2 arrival",
      "lines": [
        "The original Japanese ROM reaches (365.593,5500,-1096.803).",
        "The ordinary upper-warp arrival is (0,5500,256)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Both runs accept the warp. The control keeps the live Bob and its later nudge; only the final Crazy Box placement is omitted.",
      "endSeconds": 158,
      "firstFrame": 4380,
      "lastFrame": 4739,
      "tag": "SEPARATE ORIGINAL-JP CONTROL / ORDINARY WARP",
      "startSeconds": 146,
      "id": "comparison",
      "title": "Without the final Crazy Box",
      "lines": [
        "Omitting only the final Crazy Box still makes a gap and fresh floor 768.",
        "But it reaches the ordinary spawn without capturing the top."
      ]
    },
    {
      "footer": "Supplied: shell spawn/fake-pickup pointer/high HOLP, copied Bob state, high Mario/shell and actor positions. No later Mario edits.",
      "endSeconds": 175,
      "firstFrame": 4740,
      "lastFrame": 5249,
      "tag": "WHAT THIS FILM ESTABLISHES",
      "startSeconds": 158,
      "id": "scope",
      "title": "The handoff works; joining the route is open",
      "lines": [
        "A black Bob-omb can replace the Buddy's local job in this revised setup.",
        "Joining Mario's entry, actor delivery and timing through play is still open."
      ]
    }
  ],
